      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now let me check the scaffolding and compile script to understand the build setup.Let me check the scaffolding to understand what's available:Now I have a complete understanding. The test creates an `AlphabetConverter` that only knows the backspace character (code point 8), then tries to encode a string containing other characters, expecting an `UnsupportedEncodingException`. I'll improve readability with meaningful names, a descriptive test name, and a clarifying comment.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version replaces cryptic auto-generated variable names (`integerArray0`, `integer0`, `alphabetConverter0`) with descriptive ones (`backspaceCodePoint`, `singleCharAlphabet`, `converterWithBackspaceOnly`), removes the unused `HashMap` import, replaces the deprecated `new Integer(8)` with `Integer.valueOf(8)`, and adds a comment explaining why the encode call throws — all without changing the called methods, arguments, or expected outcome."
